@startuml eof-pipeline-outils
title EOF skill (EROOM Optimization Framework) — Tool pipeline

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
  DiamondBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  DiamondBorderColor #5BA1BC
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam ActivityBarColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #5BA1BC

start

:Source — public Google Sheet
"EOF-V.1.1 (EROOM Optimization Framework)"
9 tabs, 1 gid per tab;

note right
  Classic export endpoints (CSV/XLSX)
  fail here: 307 redirect to a
  single-use signed URL, invalid in a separate call.
  Only the gviz path works, one tab at a time.
end note

partition "**Block 1 — Retrieval** (9 calls, one per tab)" {
  :curl gviz/tq?tqx=out:json&gid=<gid>
  x9 (TO READ, Quick diagnostic,
  6 pillars, Synthesis)
  -> tmp/eof-gviz/*.json;
}

note right #C8E6C9
  "f" field (formatted) preferred over "v" (raw):
  works around a formatting bug of the
  source Sheet (criterion IDs stored as
  dates on 3 tabs, ex. 3.1 -> Date(2025,0,3)).
end note

partition "**Block 2 — build_template.py** (deterministic, no LLM calculation)" {
  :Parse the 9 JSON;
  :Tab 0 — Quick diagnostic
  Evaluation = 1 to 5 scale
  (5 text rungs per criterion);
  :Tabs 1 to 5 — Product, Architecture,
  Infrastructure, Storage, Algo & Code
  Evaluation = 5 categorical choices
  (Strength / Potential identified /
  Not applicable / To be assessed / In progress);
  :Tab 6 — Ease of change
  Evaluation = 3 DIFFERENT choices
  (Easy / Moderate effort / Hard);
  :Inject 3 hyperlinks + 2 logos
  (retrieved once from the provided Excel,
  gviz alone does not provide them);
  :Generate the table of contents + the Synthesis section
  (score formula documented in text,
  no numeric score: blank template);
  -> EOF-V.1.1 ... Full reference.md;
}

note right
  No box is pre-ticked.
  Only "Impact level" displays the fixed
  value from the reference (data, not an
  answer to give).
end note

:deliver the blank Markdown template;

stop

@enduml

@startuml eof-radar-svg
title EOF skill — generate_radar_svg.py (independent of Block 2)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam ActivityBarColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #5BA1BC

start

:Input: list (category, value 0-100)
— fictitious for a test, real once
an audit is filled in (ex. octo.com, upcoming);

partition "**generate_radar_svg.py::radar_svg()**" {
  :Compute the coordinates by trigonameetry
  (cos/sin, 1 axis every 360°/n);
  :Draw the grid — real circles
  0/25/50/75/100 % (not hexagons);
  :Draw the data polygon
  (straight lines between the points,
  navy blue #2D4675, contrast ~9.35:1);
  :Escape the text (xml.sax.saxutils.escape)
  — a raw "&" breaks the SVG rendering;
}

note right #C8E6C9
  Bug found and fixed along the way:
  unescaped "Storage & Data" broke
  the XML parsing, truncating the whole rendering
  after this label in some browsers.
end note

:-> .svg file;

stop

@enduml
